WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.701
-Our next guest is
a talented actress

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.737
you know from her work
in the TV series "Shameless,"

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:07.006
as well as films such as
"The Phantom of the Opera"

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.476
and "Mystic River."
She both executive produced

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:12.212
and stars in "Angelyne," which
is available now on Peacock.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:15.114
Let's take a look.
-So, boys, what's this about?

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:18.851
Harold tells me
you're a fan of Angelyne.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.487
Me too.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.622
-Well, as I was
just telling Harold,

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.957
your billboard
at Sunset and Vine

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.959
is in a prime location
for one of our clients.

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:28.494
-Hmm. Who's the client?

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:30.229
-We'd like to take over
the lease contract.

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:31.764
And we're willing to throw in

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.733
a couple thousand extra
to sweeten the deal.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.768
It's a very generous offer.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:40.306
-Well, gentlemen, this is not
my decision to make.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.208
Please talk to my partner.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.480
-[ Chuckles ]
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.152
-Uh, no offense, but this
might be above your head.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:01.894
-Hmm, I -- I just --
I don't see anything up there.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:05.164
-Please welcome back to
the show, Emmy Rossum, everyone.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:08.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.237
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:19.578
♪♪

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:22.382
-Hi, Emmy, welcome back.
-Hi. Thanks for having me.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.250
-This is very exciting.
Since the last time I saw you,

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.619
you are a mother
for the first time.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.920
You celebrated
your first Mother's Day.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.389
-I know. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:32.758
-Baby turning one next week?
-Yeah, on Tuesday.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.127
That was quick.
-Do you have big plans?

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.662
Big birthday plans?
-Well, you know,

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.364
she made all these friends.
-I'm so sorry.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.666
-In Central Park,
at the playground.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:42.435
Yeah, she has a busier
social calendar than I do.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.070
-That's fantastic.
-So she's having a party

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.738
with her friends --
like, a little music party.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.907
-That's excellent.
I'm very, very happy for you.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.341
Congratulations.
-Thanks.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:52.445
-So, this show --
so, this is a real person.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.879
This is a story
about a real person

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:57.950
that basically was famous
from a billboard first.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.785
Can you tell us
a little bit about her?

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:02.155
-Yeah, she's kind of
a little bit of a --

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:05.157
she's, like, a unicorn
in Los Angeles.

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:07.794
She rose to power in the '80s

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.729
through a series
of mysterious billboards

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.899
that popped up, featuring this
incredibly provocative woman,

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:16.435
kind of laying
in this provocative pose,

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:19.005
just her name and a phone number
for management.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.240
And suddenly, overnight,
they started to multiply,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.211
until there were 200 billboards
and a 10-story wall.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:28.114
And she would drive around L.A.,
and still does,

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:30.683
in this pink Corvette,
with the hair and the body

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.853
and the really
incredibly honed style.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.389
And she was the first person
to kind of raise her hand

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:40.126
and say, "I am famous.
And I am an enigma.

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.695
I am a mystery."
And to be celebrated

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:45.031
for who she is and
not something that she does.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.734
-And how old were you
when you were first hip to her,

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.236
as a thing?
-I discovered her

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.071
through her billboards
when I was 12 or 13.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.140
I was in L.A.,
auditioning for the first time,

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.777
and I saw a billboard.
And the funniest thing about it

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.346
was I -- it's almost like,
once you see it,

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:03.082
you just start
to see it everywhere.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:06.052
And so I would ask people,
"Who is this woman, Angelyne?"

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.554
And they would all be like, "Oh,
my God, Angelyne, I love her."

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.089
And I would say,
"What does she do?

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.258
Like, what's her story?"
And everyone would say

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.361
a completely different story.
She was from space.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.464
She was from Ohio.
There were 12 of her.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.900
There was some rich guy
who paid for the billboards.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.868
She was a man.
There is 12 of her.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.470
You can rent them out
for a party.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.839
They switch them out every year.
Just wild stories.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:30.310
And throughout, like,
she was so hip and smart,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.312
'cause she knew that she never
contradicted any of the stories.

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:34.713
They only fueled her fame.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:38.550
And really that was her pursuit,
the love of the world.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.887
-And so you embark on this
project to tell her story.

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:43.422
You got to meet
the real Angelyne.

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:44.891
What was that like?

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:47.593
-Yeah, I was so far down the
rabbit hole by that point.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:50.896
I was so kind of
deeply enamored of her

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:53.599
and kind of her feminine power

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:57.437
and her kind of protesting
the patriarchy in her way.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:04:01.006
I got this meeting with her

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:03.375
to talk about potentially
doing this show,

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:06.346
and I showed up an hour early,
and she was on time.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:08.448
But then, she sells merch
out of her car --

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:10.450
T-shirts and skateboards
and stuff

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.251
with her face on them,
and people buy them.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.121
They pay -- She doesn't give
selfies for free, guys.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:18.390
-Wow.
-She charges $50 for a selfie.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:20.826
And if you want the fan,
she covers her face with a fan.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.461
But if you want the fan down,
it's more.

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:23.696
-Really?
-Uh-huh.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.631
So she ended up an hour late
to the meeting,

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.867
because I could see she was,
like, swarmed with fans,

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.736
selling merch, which I loved.
-Yeah.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.937
-And then,
when she finally sat down,

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:34.140
she laid a napkin on the chair

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.942
and she kind of
delicately sat down

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.945
and kind of posed in her way.
And then she said, "So,

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:41.347
why do you have such a hard-on
to play me?"

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.548
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.650
And I was like, "That's why."

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.785
'Cause she's a real badass.
-Yeah.

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:48.954
-She is a feminist
in the most unexpected way,

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.622
and she's totally unapologetic.

00:04:50.622 --> 00:04:53.026
-You do not look like her.
-No.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:55.895
-So, to play her, obviously,

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.830
you had to go through
a transformation.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.700
I would assume
it took a great amount of time

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.802
to get into this character.
-Yes. Yes.

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:06.639
It was a very long process

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.208
with prosthetics and
a hair-and-makeup team.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:12.945
And you know,
there's kind of latex

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:15.848
and various stages of things.
-How long?

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.450
-Well, some hours in the
contemporary-day makeup

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.953
was like seven hours, some days.
-Wow!

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.789
-Yeah. So, a long time.

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:25.057
But really, they're painting you
and sculpting you

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:26.959
like you're the Sistine Chapel.
-Yeah.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.762
-Really, I mean, there was
PVC piping in my nose.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.365
There's stuff in my mouth.
My ear lobes aren't my ears.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:34.233
There's two contact lenses
in each eye.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.903
But it's so fun.
-When you look in the mirror

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.305
afterwards,
is it jarring?

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:42.040
-Well, at first it's --
You know, when they

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.877
spun me around,
it's almost like dissociative.

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.612
Like you don't see yourself,

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.881
and you're speaking in a voice
that doesn't sound like yours

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.216
and saying dialogue
that isn't yours.

00:05:51.216 --> 00:05:53.986
And it's -- At first,
it's, like, unsettling.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.555
It's terrifying.
And then it's, like,

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.223
this freedom that comes

00:05:58.223 --> 00:05:59.792
with, like,
"Oh, I can go far with this.

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:02.962
I can stretch
and I can play here.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:05.764
And this is fun."
-Really, you must feel safer

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:08.334
to take giant swings,
because it's almost feels

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.668
like you're doing it
on behalf of somebody else.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:11.704
-Yeah, and I think
what was so fun about this

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.906
is the story of,
like, talking about her,

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.108
playing her as an icon,
not a person,

00:06:16.108 --> 00:06:18.077
and all throughout history,
all the people

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:21.113
that tried to tell her story
and co-opt her narrative,

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:22.548
and so the show is kind of

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:26.318
this very unconventional
storytelling,

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:27.954
'cause she is unconventional.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:30.689
And we see
different versions of her,

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:32.425
depending on
who is telling the story.

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:34.961
So it was fun to play
all the different versions

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.262
of what she might have been.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:38.097
-Not just from other
people's perspective,

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:40.900
but over the course of 50 years.
So I would assume

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.001
you've never played a character
that has this --

00:06:43.001 --> 00:06:44.203
-No.
-As far as the amount of years

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.071
the scope was.
-No, aging in both directions.

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:48.374
-Right.
-Tape and string.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:50.543
[ Laughter ]
Yep.

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:52.678
-Your husband, Sam,
who's a very talented

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.480
television producer and writer,
he was a producer

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.481
on this, as well.
-He was.

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:57.316
-Have you guys --
What was it like,

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:59.585
collaborating with him on this?
-It was so fun.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:03.656
Although, he did come to set and
did not know what to make of it,

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:05.758
'cause it was just not me
anymore.

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.860
-Yeah.
-But, you know,

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.328
you rehearse something
for so long,

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:12.698
you do it more hours of the day
than you're not doing it.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:14.533
So, you come home
and you're making eggs

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:16.269
at the end of the day
for, like, a quick dinner,

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:18.438
and you find yourself
kind of doing

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:20.673
all this stuff
that's so foreign to you.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.008
But you're not in it anymore,
but you're still in it.

00:07:23.008 --> 00:07:24.510
-Yeah.
-So, it's just this --

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.447
Yeah, it kind of permeates
your home life a bit.

00:07:28.447 --> 00:07:30.750
-You worked with
a parakeet, correct?

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.251
-Yes.
-How was that?

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:34.921
-You know,
I like making it hard.

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.255
-Yeah.
-I really do.

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:38.591
It's always fun.
-Was the parakeet hard?

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:40.926
-Most professional actor
I've ever worked with.

00:07:40.926 --> 00:07:42.294
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:07:42.294 --> 00:07:44.963
Hit their mark
every single time.

00:07:44.963 --> 00:07:47.733
Had been in movies,
well-trained, yeah.

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:50.236
-Did you retroactively
think less

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:51.670
of the human actors
you'd worked with,

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:52.738
every time
you worked with the parakeet?

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:54.906
-Less of myself.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.906 --> 00:07:59.145
No, I think it's so fun
to work with animals.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:01.914
I think, anytime -- I like to
eat in scenes, too, though.

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:04.550
I like to be challenged.
-Yeah, do it all.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:07.353
Hey, congratulations.
It is such a unique show.

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:08.954
And it's really cool
that you told this story.

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:10.055
And thanks so much
for being here.

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:11.089
-Thank you.
-Always such a pleasure.

00:08:11.089 --> 00:08:12.858
You guys, Emmy Rossum!

00:08:12.858 --> 00:08:15.528
All episodes of "Angelyne"
are available now on Peacock.

